# Where the JDK for CICFlowMeter lives.
#
# One path per line; the first line that holds a usable JDK wins. Blank
# lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Read by get_java_home() in
# backend/app/utils/runtime_paths.py.
#
# The JDK is NOT unpacked into tools/ because this project tree is inside
# OneDrive: a JDK is ~192 MB across 444 files and syncing all of it to
# cloud storage buys nothing. It sits on the local disk beside the other
# build tools this service already calls -- CICFlowMeter and Maven are
# both under C:\Tools -- and this file records where.
#
# Installed 23 September 2026: Temurin OpenJDK 1.8.0_504-b01 (x64),
# unpacked from Downloads/OpenJDK8U-jdk_x64_windows_hotspot_8u504b01.zip.
# JDK 8 is required because CICFlowMeter's pom.xml compiles with
# source/target 1.8 and JDK 24 removed -source 8.

C:\Tools\jdk8u504-b01
